          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "{\n \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\",\n \"name\": \"Tides.lean\",\n \"url\": \"https://uuidna.com/lean/Tides.lean\",\n \"inLanguage\": \"lean4\",\n \"variableMeasured\": {\n  \"@type\": \"PropertyValue\",\n  \"name\": \"theorems\",\n  \"value\": 6,\n  \"unitText\": \"theorem\"\n }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-rule_of_twelfths",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The sailor's rule of twelfths: over six hours a tide rises 1,2,3,3,2,1 twelfths of its range — and 1+2+3+3+2+1 = 12, the whole range accounted for."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 12"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem rule_of_twelfths : 1 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 12 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-twelfths_symmetric",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The rule is a palindrome — [1,2,3,3,2,1] reversed is itself: flood and ebb mirror, the tide fills as it drains."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "[1,2,3,3,2,1].reverse = [1,2,3,3,2,1]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem twelfths_symmetric : [1,2,3,3,2,1].reverse = [1,2,3,3,2,1] := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-half_tide_at_hour_three",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "By the third hour the water stands at HALF its range: 1+2+3 = 6 of 12 (2·6 = 12) — half-tide falls at mid-flood."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1 + 2 + 3 = 6 ∧ 2 * 6 = 12"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem half_tide_at_hour_three : 1 + 2 + 3 = 6 ∧ 2 * 6 = 12 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-semidiurnal_period",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Two high tides fall a lunar day apart: 12h25m = 745 minutes each, and 745·2 = 1490 = 24h50m — the semidiurnal rhythm, set by the Moon."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "745 * 2 = 1490"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem semidiurnal_period : 745 * 2 = 1490 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-spring_exceeds_neap",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A spring tide (new or full Moon, Sun and Moon aligned, their pulls ADD) exceeds a neap (at the quarter, pulls partly cancel): 2+1 > 2−1 — the range swells and shrinks with the phase."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2 + 1 > 2 - 1"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem spring_exceeds_neap : 2 + 1 > 2 - 1 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-flood_and_ebb",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "One semidiurnal cycle is six hours of flood and six of ebb: 6 + 6 = 12 — the tide gives back exactly the hours it took."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6 + 6 = 12"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem flood_and_ebb : 6 + 6 = 12 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
